00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.280
You maintain around 80 open source

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.239
projects. How do you manage it all?

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:06.080
>> Not very well. Uh so

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.960
I like to approach maintaining my own

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.200
personal libraries as a bunch of micro

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.360
repos. Uh I found working with monor

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.840
repos in the past to be

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.759
convenient in some ways, but you need a

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:19.520
