00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.840
make it work for Yelp. uh Yelp had

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.440
Python, SCSS, and JavaScript developers

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.160
at the time. And we wanted a way to

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.199
eliminate a 30,000line bash script that

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:36.960
had so many bugs uh so many problems

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.720
with a more easy to manage Python tool

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.720
uh that installed in those various

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.240
programming languages so that people

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.600
didn't have to worry about setting up

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.520
their development environments. So you

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.520
mentioned various programming languages.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.720
Um as most of us using premit know that

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.639
pre-commit supports many different

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:57.199
languages. What were the the hardest

00:04:57.199 --> 00:04:59.040
technical challenges you faced when you

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.720
were developing it? Was it supporting

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.199
many different languages or something

00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:05.199
>> Yes, it's definitely the languages. So

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:06.800
when PMIT started out it was just

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.880
Python, Ruby and JavaScript and no other

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.080
major tools. Uh, but now it supports I

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.360
think 13 different programming languages

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.759
and by far keeping up with all of the

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:21.440
different ecosystems is the hardest

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.080
part. I think some ecosystems are easier

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.840
than others. Like Python is actually

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.199
pretty easy. You set up a virtual

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:29.680
environment, you pip install. Uh, Ruby

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.680
also fairly straightforward. You know,

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.120
you have your gem, you gem install. uh

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.039
Go has gone through at least three

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:39.199
different iterations of how they want to

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:42.400
install things and tools and libraries

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.479
and how to separate those apart. I think

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:47.840
Go is probably the most complicated or

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.160
the most complicated to keep up with.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.720
>> Uh other languages have various ideas

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.440
about how installation should work. I

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.680
think R is probably the weirdest one,

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.320
